# status: draft (Phase 8b, 2026-11-07), waiting for the owner's approval
# Trial shrines (DIALOGUE_DESIGN.md §10 `trial_gust_intro` / `_complete`). The Gust Trial at the Windcall Shrine
# (draft name), east of the old shrine ruins: started by TrialShrine (data/trials/gust_trial.tres). The shrine speaks
# as an old, slow voice; it calls Aurelia "lantern-bearer". Owner decision 2026-11-07: hidden runes, lit in order
# (one curl, two, three), then a ring of wind with two short waves of enemies.
# Only GameState, QuestManager, Inventory, PlayerData, DragonManager, Cutscene and AudioManager may be called.

~ trial_gust_intro
Shrine: [#calm] ...A lantern-bearer. It has been long since one came this way.
Shrine: Wind is born from stillness. Wake my runes as the wind is born: one breath, then two, then three.
Lumen: The runes are sleeping in the mist. Your Lantern Glow can find them.
Aurelia: [#thinking] One curl, then two, then three... Like counting breaths. I can do that.
=> END

~ trial_gust_test
Shrine: [#calm] The runes remember. Now stand in the wind, lantern-bearer, and do not fall.
=> END

~ trial_gust_complete
Shrine: [#pleased] You stood. The wind is yours to call. Take it.
Aurelia: [#excited] A spell tome! Gust! My third spell! That's half again as many spells as this morning!
Lumen: Read it at a Lantern Shrine. Then the wind will listen.
=> END

~ trial_gust_repeat
Shrine: [#calm] The wind remembers you, lantern-bearer.
=> END
